{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792187375,"nonce":"yQIOi729GEs1DFASRXva1l+wjxU=","title":"pointerEvents None on an element hides its whole subtree from the pointer, even children set to Auto","message":"**What happens**\n\nA `\u003cdiv pointerEvents={PointerEvents.None}\u003e` wrapper with a child `pointerEvents={PointerEvents.Auto}` that has `onPointerEnter`: the child never receives the event. blinc_abi's hit test (`src/hit.rs`, `hit_inner`) returns as soon as a node is in `tree.pass_through`, before visiting its children.\n\n**What CSS does**\n\n`pointer-events` is inherited: children of a `none` element are also `none` by default, but a descendant that sets `auto` itself is a hit target again. Blinc's own router (`blinc_layout/src/event_router.rs`) also tests children before applying `pointer_events_none` to the node itself.\n\n**Reproducer**\n\nA full-width absolute overlay with `pointerEvents={None}` holding a centred bar with `pointerEvents={Auto}` and hover handlers, driven by `Pointer.move` over the bar: no enter fires. The README banner's island (tools/snapshot/scenes/Island.hx) hit this and works round it by putting the bar in a zero-size absolute box instead, as ChimpMonk's NotchMenu slot does.\n\n**Fix**\n\nDistinguish an explicit `Auto` from the inherited default: pass through a `None` node's own box but keep testing its children, each passing through unless it, or a nearer ancestor, sets `Auto`.","files":null}]}